statement:
Let n ≥ 1, x ∈ ℝⁿ (ℝⁿ = Euclid n), ρ > 0, K ∈ ℝ, and let u : ℝⁿ → ℝ satisfy:
- u is differentiable at x;
- u is continuous on closedBall(x, 3ρ/2), and |u(z)| ≤ K for all z ∈ closedBall(x, 3ρ/2);
- u satisfies the ball mean value identity ∫_{B̆_ρ(z)} u = (volume (ball z ρ)).toReal·u(z) for every z ∈ closedBall(x, ρ/2).
Then ‖Du(x)‖ ≤ 2nK/ρ, where Du(x) = fderiv ℝ u x and ‖·‖ is the operator norm.
